WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.724
Post an opening once.

00:00:01.724 --> 00:00:03.899
Volunteers nearby swipe right.

00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:08.320
You say yes, and after the shift one tap confirms their hours.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:16.070
Jordan says the nonprofit confirms hours, then posts an opening in one short form, written once.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:22.428
Each card says why it's shown: close by, free Saturday morning, confirms hours.

00:00:22.428 --> 00:00:23.920
Riley taps the heart.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.945
Jordan says yes and says hi.

00:00:26.945 --> 00:00:30.200
On Riley's phone, it's a match, with no tap.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.350
Riley taps Say hi, reads Jordan's message, and replies.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:42.380
After the shift, Jordan marks Riley attended in one tap, with the hours already filled in.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:50.600
Riley gets a certificate for Silver Lake Garden Friends: every confirmed shift, the total, a signature code.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.770
Anyone with the link can check that it's genuine, with no sign-in: same nonprofit, same total.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:00:59.588
Causematch.

00:00:59.588 --> 00:01:01.746
Nonprofits post and say yes.

00:01:01.746 --> 00:01:03.086
Volunteers swipe.

00:01:03.086 --> 00:01:05.690
Join the Los Angeles County pilot.
